---
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import sust from "../../assets/sust.png";
---

<Layout title="Sustainable Cities">
  <main class="page-container">
    
    <!-- HERO SECTION -->
    <section class="theme-hero-section">
      <div class="hero-content">
        <h1>Sustainable Cities</h1>
        <p>
          Investigating sustainability principles in buildings and cities.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="hero-image-container">
        <img
          src={sust.src}
          alt="Sustainable Cities"
          class="hero-icon"
        />
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- STICKY SUB-NAV BAR -->
    <nav class="sub-nav-bar">
      <div class="sub-nav-links">
        <a href="#independent" class="sub-nav-item">
          Independent Research <span class="count">3</span>
        </a>
        <a href="#collaborative" class="sub-nav-item">
          Collaborative Research <span class="count">3</span>
        </a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <!-- SECTION 1: Independent Research (Clean: No Tags) -->
    
    <div class="content-grid" id="independent">
      <aside class="sidebar">
        <h2>Independent Research</h2>
      </aside>

      <div class="project-list">
        <!-- Project 1 Book Chapter -->
        <div class="project-card">
        <span class="mono-date">2026</span> 
          <h3>
            <a href="https://www.routledge.com/Smart-and-Innovative-Solutions-for-a-Net-Zero-Built-Environment/Senaratne-Domingo-Perera/p/book/9781041256892" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">    
           Smart and Innovative Solutions for a Net-Zero Built Environment</a>
          </h3>
          <p>
          Overall, the book aims to bring together leading-edge smart solutions that consider both embodied and 
          operational carbon reduction throughout the building lifecycle in its drive to achieve net-zero carbon.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Project 2 -->
        <div class="project-card">
        <span class="mono-date">2025</span> 
          <h3>
            <a href="https://docs.lib.purdue.edu/cgi/viewcontent.cgi?article=1740&context=cib-conferences" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">    
           What is Stopping Building Information Modeling (BIM)-based Whole Life Carbon Assessment of Buildings in Hong Kong? </a>
          </h3>
          <p>
          How do researchers, construction professionals, and experts perceive BIM-based WLCA differently and why? 
          We collected data from 80 Hong Kong-based practitioners to conduct statistical and factor analysis.
          </p>
        </div>

        <!-- Project 2 -->
        <div class="project-card">
        <span class="mono-date">2025</span>
          <h3>
            <a href="https://ascelibrary.org/doi/10.1061/9780784486436.083" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">    
            Digital Twins for Sustainable Hospitality Facilities Management: A Review and Empirical Investigation
            </a>
          </h3>
          <p>
          How can we enhance sustainability facilities management in hotels without sacrificing guests' experiences?
          We investigated the role of Digital Twin in assisting hoteliers to address sustainability challenges.
          </p>
        </div>
        </div>
    </div>

<!-- SECTION 2: Collaborative Research (Structured Bullets) -->
    <div class="content-grid" id="collaborative">
      <aside class="sidebar">
        <h2>Collaborative Research</h2>
      </aside>

      <div class="project-list">
    
<!-- 1. XDT -->
    <div class="project-card">      
    <span class="mono-date">2026</span>
    <h3>
    <a href="https://www.mdpi.com/2075-5309/16/10/1856" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
    Explainable Digital Twins for Urban Drainage Resilience: A Multi-Source TCN-LSTM Framework for Real-Time Water Flow Prediction
    </a>
    </h3>

    <p>
    Urban drainage systems (UDSs) are increasingly challenged by short-duration extreme rainfall, aging infrastructure, and rising surcharge risk. 
    Physics-based hydrodynamic models are widely used for system assessment, but their high computational cost limits real-time operational prediction.
    An explainable Digital Twin is developed for a separate sewer network in the Yangtze River Delta, China. 
  </p>
    
    <ul class="structured-bullets">
    <li><strong>Role & Affiliation:</strong> Co-author, University of Cambridge and Zhejiang University.</li>
    <li><strong>Project Scope:</strong> A hybrid TCN-LSTM model was developed to predict water level and surcharge risk probability at 15–60 min lead times. 
    A surrogate-based SHAP module was used to explain model predictions at the node and subcatchment scales.</li>
    <li><strong>Key Contributions:</strong> Assisted in designing Explainable Digital Twins.</li>
    </ul>
    
    </div>

<!-- 2.SunYi-Exergame -->
    <div class="project-card">
    <span class="mono-date">2023-2024</span>
      <h3>
    <a href="https://www.ntu.edu.sg/arise/research-focus/health-coaching---lifestyleintervention/applying-immersive-projector-with-exergames-a-pilot-study-for-older-adults-in-singapore" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
    Applying Immersive Projector with Exergames: A Pilot Study for Older Adults in Singapore
    </a>
    </h3>

    <p>
    In collaboration with Lion Befrienders Singapore (LB), we propose using exergames to promote a sustainable lifestyle in Singapore and Hong Kong's aging population.
    </p>
  
    <ul class="structured-bullets">
    <li><strong>Role & Affiliation:</strong> Part-time Research Assistant, 
        Nanyang Technological University/Hong Kong Polytechnic University; 
        Co-Principal Investigator: <a href="https://www.polyu.edu.hk/cmi/people/academic-staff/dr-sun-yi/" target="_blank" 
        rel="noopener noreferrer" class="external-link"> Dr SUN Yi </a>, the Hong Kong Polytechnic University.
    
    </li>
    
    <li><strong>Project Scope:</strong> Creating serious exergames with physical activities and data-mining capabilities to engage the older adults in daily activities in both the senior centre settings and home settings.</li>
    <li><strong>Key Contributions:</strong> Carried out immersive exergame experiments and questionnaire surveys with the elderly.</li>
    </ul>

  </div>

<!-- 3.SunYi-PersonEnvtFit -->
<div class="project-card">
<span class="mono-date">2020-2021</span>  
  <h3>
    <a href="https://www.cepu.gov.hk/doc/en/research_report(PDF)/2019.A6.145.19D_Final%20Report_Dr%20Sun.pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">
    Effects of Environment-related Experiences on Older Person’s Well-being in Hong Kong’s “Double Ageing” Context:
    A Person–environment Perspective
    </a>
  </h3>
    
    <p>
    A conceptual framework that articulates the co-constitution of socio-spatial
  experience, psychological experience, and well-being is developed to explain the mechanism underlying the
  associations between socio-spatial experience and well-being.
    </p>
    
    <ul class="structured-bullets">
    <li><strong>Role & Affiliation:</strong> Part-time Research Assistant, 
        Hong Kong SAR Public Policy Research Funding Scheme; 
        Principal Investigator: <a href="https://www.polyu.edu.hk/cmi/people/academic-staff/dr-sun-yi/" target="_blank" 
        rel="noopener noreferrer" class="external-link"> Dr SUN Yi </a>, the Hong Kong Polytechnic University.
    </li>
    
    <li><strong>Project Scope:</strong> Applying a mixed-method approach to
      assess the effects of socio-spatial and psychological experiences on well-being, and
      examine the mediating effects of psychological experiences.</li>
    <li><strong>Key Contributions:</strong> Collected empirical data from 501 questionnaires within 2 categories of Tertiary Planning Units in Hong Kong. 
      Assisted in data pre-processing before research analysis.</li>
    </ul>
        
    </div>
    </div>
    </div>
  </main>
</Layout>

<style>
  /* =========================================
     1. PAGE LAYOUT & GEOMETRY
     ========================================= */
  .page-container {
    max-width: 1200px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 0 2rem 4rem;
  }

  /* =========================================
     2. HERO SECTION (Side-by-Side)
     ========================================= */
  .theme-hero-section {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    gap: 4rem;
    padding: 4rem 0 1.5rem;
  }

  .hero-content {
    flex: 1;
    max-width: 650px;
  }

  .hero-content h1 {
    font-size: 3rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
    color: #111;
  }

  .hero-content p {
    font-size: 1.2rem;
    color: #555;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin: 0;
  }

  .hero-image-container {
    flex-shrink: 0;
    width: 240px;
  }

  .hero-icon {
    width: 100%;
    height: auto;
    object-fit: contain;
  }

  /* =========================================
     3. STICKY SUB-NAVIGATION BAR
     ========================================= */
  .sub-nav-bar {
    position: sticky;
    top: 0;
    background: rgba(250, 248, 245, 0.95); /* Slight transparency */
    backdrop-filter: blur(10px);           /* Blurs content behind it */
    z-index: 100;
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5;
    padding: 1rem 0;
    margin-bottom: 3.5rem;
  }

  .sub-nav-links {
    display: flex;
    gap: 2.5rem;
  }

  .sub-nav-item {
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    color: #666;
    text-decoration: none;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 0.5rem;
    transition: color 0.2s;
  }

  .sub-nav-item:hover {
    color: #0067c0;
  }

  .sub-nav-item .count {
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    background: #e5e5e5;
    color: #555;
    padding: 0.1rem 0.4rem;
    border-radius: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* =========================================
     4. CONTENT GRIDS (Sidebar + List)
     ========================================= */
  .content-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 260px 1fr;
    gap: 4rem;
    padding-bottom: 2rem;       
    margin-bottom: 2rem;        
    border-bottom: 1px solid #e5e5e5; 
    scroll-margin-top: 6rem; /* Ensures sticky nav doesn't cover title when clicked */
  }

  .content-grid:last-of-type {
    border-bottom: none;
    padding-bottom: 0;
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }

  .sidebar h2 {
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: #222;
    position: sticky;
    top: 5rem;
    margin: -0.2rem 0 0 0;
  }

  /* =========================================
     5. PROJECT CARDS & TYPOGRAPHY
     ========================================= */
  .project-card {
    padding: 2.5rem 0;
    border-top: 1px solid #e5e5e5;
  }
  
  .project-card:first-child {
    border-top: none;
    padding-top: 0;
  }

  .project-card h3 {
    margin: 0 0 0.75rem;
  }

  .project-card h3 a {
    color: #0067c0;
    text-decoration: none;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3;
  }

  .project-card h3 a:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
  }

  .project-card p {
    color: #444;
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* =========================================
     6. COLLAB LISTS & LINKS (New Updates)
     ========================================= */
  .structured-bullets {
    margin: 1.25rem 0 0 0;
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    list-style-type: square;
  }

  .structured-bullets li {
    font-size: 0.95rem;
    color: #555;
    line-height: 1.6;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }

  .structured-bullets strong {
    color: #222;
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  /* The Specific "Academic Blue" Link Style for LLM+ */
  .external-link {
    color: #0067c0;  /* Matches Main Title Blue exactly */
    font-weight: 700;
    text-decoration: none;
  }

  .external-link:hover {
    text-decoration: underline;
    color: #004b99;
  }

  /* =========================================
     7. MOBILE RESPONSIVE
     ========================================= */
  @media (max-width: 900px) {
    .theme-hero-section {
      flex-direction: column-reverse; /* Stacks image on top */
      align-items: flex-start;
      gap: 2rem;
      padding: 3rem 0 1rem;
    }

    .content-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr; /* Stacks sidebar above list */
      gap: 1rem;
    }

    .sidebar h2 {
      position: static;
      border-bottom: 2px solid #eee;
      padding-bottom: 0.5rem;
      margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    }
  }
  .mono-date {
  font-family: monospace; /* Technical feel */
  font-size: 0.85rem;
  color: #888;            /* Subtle Grey */
  font-weight: 500;
  display: block;
  margin-bottom: 0.5rem;  /* Space between date and title */
  letter-spacing: 0.05em;
}

/* Ensure the title spacing is tight */
.project-card h3 {
  margin-top: 0;
  line-height: 1.35;
}
</style>
